# dependencies
node_modules

# build output
dist
dist-ssr

# env — secrets & config, never commit (values live in Vercel)
.env
.env.*.local

# Firebase Admin SDK service-account keys — full bypass-the-rules access,
# never commit. Catches this project's key regardless of exact filename.
service account.json
service-account*.json
serviceAccount*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json

# electron-builder's packaged installer/output. ARTIFACTS only — the
# desktop app's SOURCE is deliberately tracked: electron/ (main.cjs,
# preload.cjs, local-db/), build/ (icon.ico, installer.nsh, the installer
# sidebars) and scripts/ (the generators for those assets). Vercel never
# looks at any of it, so it costs nothing to deploy, and keeping it in the
# repo is what makes the desktop build reproducible on another machine
# instead of existing only on one laptop.
release
# electron-builder's staging dir. Windows Defender can hold a lock on this
# mid-extraction and leave it behind after a failed build (see BUILD.md
# §19) — never commit a half-extracted Electron runtime.
release/win-unpacked.tmp

# Local build scratch — the alternate output dir used when release/ is
# locked.
/gymos-release

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Claude Code's local tool-permission state — machine-specific absolute
# paths and scratch-file allowances, useful to nobody else and not part of
# the app.
.claude/

# editor / os
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.local
